# 🏆 World Cup On Top — Analyst Prompt

You are my World Cup analyst. Research EVERYTHING about the currently running FIFA World Cup 2026 and build me ONE beautiful, modern, print-ready PDF titled **"World Cup On Top"** — a full dedicated page for EVERY team, but **lighter and far better looking** than the bloated, pale version you made last time. ⚽

📄 **FINAL DELIVERABLE:** a single multi-page PDF named `World Cup On Top.pdf`. PDF only.

---

## ⚠️ READ THIS FIRST — why the last PDF looked pale, and how to fix it

The last output was washed-out because **print renderers silently DROP color emoji and flag glyphs.** Every 🏳️ flag, ⚽/🅰️/🟡/🔴 badge and ✅ status pill you were told to add rendered as a blank gap or bare text. Do NOT let that happen again. Pick ONE rendering path:

**Path A (preferred) — headless Chromium.** Render with Playwright or Puppeteer `page.pdf({ format: 'A4', printBackground: true })`. Chromium draws color emoji + flags natively. `printBackground:true` is mandatory or every colored band/tile/pill renders white.

**Path B — weasyprint / wkhtmltopdf.** These cannot draw color emoji. So replace EVERY emoji and flag with an inline **Twemoji SVG image**:
- Convert the emoji to lowercase hex codepoints, strip any `fe0f`, join multi-codepoint sequences with `-`.
  - 🇸🇦 → `1f1f8-1f1e6`, ⚽ → `26bd`, 🏆 → `1f3c6`, 🟡 → `1f7e1`, 🔴 → `1f534`, ✅ → `2705`, 🅰️ → `1f170`
- Fetch `https://raw.githubusercontent.com/twitter/twemoji/master/assets/svg/{code}.svg`
- Inline it as `<img src="data:image/svg+xml;base64,…">` (base64 the SVG). Render flags inside a small white rounded chip so they pop on colored bands.

Either way: **test-render 1 team page and visually confirm flags/badges actually appear before generating all 48.**

---

## 📏 SIZE RULES — make it LIGHTER than last time

Last build was ~66 pages and full of dead weight. New constraints:

1. **One page per team = HARD CAP.** Exactly one A4 page each. NEVER spill a team to a second page — trim content to fit (see template). 48 teams = ~48 pages; that is the floor, everything else is overhead to cut.
2. **No divider/section-break pages.** Zero standalone dividers. Put the section title inline at the top of the next content page.
3. **Merge the overhead sections** (this is where the page savings come from):
   - Cover (1) · Contents (1)
   - **Tournament Overview** (1 page) = snapshot dashboard **+** host cities/stadiums combined.
   - **Group Standings** (1–2 pages) = all groups, compact tables.
   - **Leaderboards** (1 page) = top scorers **+** assists **+** discipline + missed pens, all on one page.
   - **Win Probability Ranking** (1 page) = top-3 cards + full ranked table (fold the team-stats master table into this page or drop it).
   - **Upcoming Fixtures** (1 page, next round only) · **Methodology** (1 page).
   - Knockout bracket: 1 page **only if** the stage has been reached, else skip entirely.
4. **Near-zero prose.** Badges, tiles and tables do the talking. Max 1–2 lines of text per team. No paragraphs anywhere.
5. **Target: ~52–56 pages total.** 

🔻 **Optional "ultra-light" toggle:** if I say "ultra-light", render ELIMINATED teams as 2-up half-pages (two teams per page) and keep full pages only for teams still in contention. That drops it another ~15–20 pages. Default = full page for every team.

---

## 🎨 DESIGN SYSTEM — vivid, not pale (use these exact values)

**Palette (hex, no vague color names):**
- Page background `#F3F6F4` · ink text `#14181A`
- Chrome / pitch green: deep `#00471F`, base `#006C35`, bright `#0E8A47`
- Semantic: win `#16A34A` · draw `#F59E0B` · loss `#DC2626`
- Stat-tile tints: mint `#E8F6EE` · rose `#FCEBEC` · slate `#EEF2F5` · amber `#FEF4E3` · sky `#E9F2FB` · plum `#F1ECF8`
- Cards: white `#FFFFFF`, border `#E6ECE8`, soft shadow `0 1.5mm 5mm rgba(16,40,28,.08)`

**Header band (per team):** FULL-BLEED gradient `linear-gradient(115deg, deep → base → bright)`, **tinted with that nation's two flag colors** (fallback = pitch green). White text. Large flag chip + big team name on the left; group tag + FIFA-rank tag + status pill on the right.

**Spacing (let it breathe):** A4, full-bleed band via `@page { margin:0 }` + inner padding `16mm`; ~`6mm` gutters; card padding `5–6mm`; radius `4–5mm`; repeating footer pinned to the bottom of every page.

**Components (any number that CAN be a pill/chip/tile/bar SHOULD be one):**
- Status pill: ✅ QUALIFIED (green `#16A34A`) · ⏳ IN CONTENTION (amber) · ❌ ELIMINATED (gray) · 🏆 CHAMPION (gold). Rounded, bold, soft shadow.
- Form chip: 9mm square, white bold letter — W green · D amber · L red.
- Stat tile: icon + big bold number (24pt) + 7pt UPPERCASE letter-spaced label, on a tinted background. **Color the number** green when good, red when bad (negative GD = red).
- Win-probability bar: rounded track `#E9EFEB` + gradient fill `linear-gradient(90deg,#0B6B3A,#37C871)` + bold % label.
- Micro-badges: ⚽ ×N · 🅰️ ×N · 🟡 ×N · 🔴 ×N as little rounded chips.
- Tables: pitch-green header row, white rows with `#FAFCFB` zebra striping, result chips (W/D/L) in a Result column.

**Drop-in CSS foundation** (reuse these classes; only inject data + per-nation band colors):

```css
@page { size:A4; margin:0; }
* { margin:0; padding:0; box-sizing:border-box; }
body { font-family:'Inter','Helvetica Neue',Arial,sans-serif; color:#14181A; }
.page { width:210mm; min-height:297mm; background:#F3F6F4; position:relative; }

/* header band — swap the two greens for the nation's flag colors */
.band { background:linear-gradient(115deg,#00471F,#006C35 55%,#0E8A47); color:#fff;
        padding:8mm 16mm 6mm; position:relative; overflow:hidden; }
.flagwrap { width:21mm; height:21mm; border-radius:4mm; background:#fff;
            box-shadow:0 3mm 7mm rgba(0,0,0,.28); display:flex; align-items:center; justify-content:center; }
.tname { font-size:30pt; font-weight:bold; letter-spacing:-.5pt; line-height:1; }
.pill { font-size:9pt; font-weight:bold; padding:2.4mm 5mm; border-radius:20mm;
        text-transform:uppercase; display:inline-flex; align-items:center; gap:1.6mm; }
.pill.qual { background:#16A34A; color:#fff; box-shadow:0 2mm 5mm rgba(22,163,74,.45); }

/* cards + hero */
.body { padding:5mm 16mm 0; }
.card { background:#fff; border-radius:5mm; border:.3mm solid #E6ECE8;
        box-shadow:0 1.5mm 5mm rgba(16,40,28,.08); }
.barfill { height:5mm; border-radius:5mm; background:linear-gradient(90deg,#0B6B3A,#37C871); }

/* form chips */
.chip { width:9mm; height:9mm; border-radius:2.4mm; color:#fff; font-weight:bold;
        display:flex; align-items:center; justify-content:center; }
.cW{background:#16A34A} .cD{background:#F59E0B} .cL{background:#DC2626}

/* stat tiles */
.grid { display:grid; grid-template-columns:repeat(6,1fr); gap:3mm; }
.tile { border-radius:4mm; padding:3mm 2.5mm; text-align:center; }
.tile .num { font-size:19pt; font-weight:bold; line-height:1; }
.tile .lbl { font-size:6.6pt; letter-spacing:.8pt; text-transform:uppercase; color:#6B7A72; font-weight:bold; }
.t-mint{background:#E8F6EE} .t-rose{background:#FCEBEC} .t-slate{background:#EEF2F5}
.t-amber{background:#FEF4E3} .t-sky{background:#E9F2FB} .t-plum{background:#F1ECF8}
.pos{color:#16A34A} .neg{color:#DC2626}

/* tables */
table { width:100%; border-collapse:collapse; background:#fff; border-radius:4mm; overflow:hidden; }
th { background:#0B6B3A; color:#fff; font-size:7pt; text-transform:uppercase; text-align:left; padding:2.4mm 3.5mm; }
td { font-size:9pt; padding:2.4mm 3.5mm; border-top:.3mm solid #EEF2F0; }
tr:nth-child(even) td { background:#FAFCFB; }
.rc { font-size:7.5pt; font-weight:bold; color:#fff; padding:1mm 2.6mm; border-radius:10mm; }
.rcW{background:#16A34A} .rcD{background:#F59E0B} .rcL{background:#DC2626}

/* footer pinned to bottom of every page */
.foot { position:absolute; left:0; right:0; bottom:0; background:#0B6B3A; color:#fff;
        padding:4mm 16mm; display:flex; justify-content:space-between; font-size:8pt; }
```

---

## 🔍 RESEARCH (keep the DATA exhaustive — only the PDF gets lighter)

First run `date +%F`. Then confirm WC 2026 is running, which stage we're in, and what's been played.

Pull, cross-checked against 2+ sources (FIFA.com first, then ESPN / BBC / Guardian / Reuters / AP / Transfermarkt / FBref / WhoScored; on conflict FIFA wins): host cities + stadiums; format + advancement rules; every group's standings (P W D L GF GA GD Pts); every match played (date, city, stadium, score incl. ET/pens, scorers + minute, 🟡/🔴 cards, possession/shots/fouls/corners/pass-acc); tournament-wide top scorers + assists + cards + missed pens + each team's key player; per-team totals (GF, GA, clean sheets, possession %, pass acc %, fouls, cards, pen record); upcoming fixtures; and a defensible **win-probability %** per team still in contention (form + GD + opponent quality + history + any bookmaker odds, with one line of reasoning). **Never invent a stat — unavailable after cross-checking = "—", logged in Methodology.**

---

## 📑 PAGE ORDER (trimmed)

1. 🏆 Cover (full-bleed, title + tournament/host/stage + one hero number + date)
2. 📋 Contents (every section + every team page, anchored)
3. 📊 Tournament Overview (snapshot tiles **+** host cities/stadiums)
4. 📈 Group Standings (compact tables, status pills inline, qualified bold, eliminated struck-through)
5. 🥇 Knockout Bracket — only if reached
6. **👤 Per-team pages** — one full page each. Order: in-contention by win % (high→low), then eliminated by final standing. Every team appears.
7. ⚽ Leaderboards (top scorers **+** assists **+** discipline **+** missed pens, one page)
8. 🏆 Win Probability Ranking (top-3 cards + full ranked table; fold team-stats master here)
9. 📅 Upcoming Fixtures (next round only)
10. 📝 Methodology (sources, data date, "estimates not guarantees", "—" gaps)

---

## 👤 PER-TEAM PAGE TEMPLATE (one page, no overflow)

- **Header band** (nation-tinted): 🏳️ flag chip + TEAM NAME · right: [Group tag] [FIFA-rank tag] [Status pill]
- **Hero row:** 🏆 Win Probability — big % + gradient bar · Form strip — W/D/L chips (last 3)
- **Stat tile grid (6 cols):** GP · GF · GA · GD · Clean Sheets · Possession % · Pass Acc % · Fouls · 🟡 · 🔴 · Pens Scored · Pens Missed (color numbers good/bad)
- **⭐ Key player callout:** name · position · one line why · ⚽/🅰️ micro-badges
- **Two compact tables side by side:** Team Top Scorers (Player · ⚽ · 🅰️ · Min, top 3) | Match by Match (Opponent · Score · Result chip · Scorers, last 3, reverse-chrono)
- **Footer:** "World Cup On Top 🏆 · Data as of <date> · <team> · page N"

---

## ⛔ HARD RULES
- One team = exactly one full page. Trim to fit, never spill, never shrink the whole page to cram.
- No divider pages. Merge overhead sections as listed. Target ~52–56 pages.
- Render via Path A or B above and **verify flags/badges actually appear** before generating all teams. `printBackground:true` if Chromium.
- Cross-check scorers & standings 2+ sources; FIFA wins conflicts. No invented stats — "—" + log it.

## ✅ WHEN DONE, tell me:
1. Who's leading the tournament (or who won).
2. The biggest surprise/upset so far.
3. The team with the highest calculated win chance + the %.
4. Total PDF page count + confirm every team has its own page (and that flags/badges rendered).

